---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import ComingSoon from '../../components/ComingSoon.astro';
---

<Base
  title="Benchmarks"
  description="What we measure (action detection, temporal localization, QA with timestamps), against which baselines, and honest failure modes."
  canonicalPath="/technology/benchmarks"
  mdTwin="/technology/benchmarks.md"
>
  <div class="page">
    <a class="back" href="/technology">← Technology</a>
    <section class="hero">
      <p class="eyebrow">Technology</p>
      <h1>Benchmarks</h1>
      <p class="lede">
        What we measure, against which baselines, and honest failure modes.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="content">
      <p>
        Our benchmark suite covers three capability dimensions: action detection (does
        the model correctly identify that a given action occurred?), temporal localization
        (does it know when — with timestamps?), and question-answering with timestamps
        (can it answer open-ended questions about video content and cite the evidence?).
        We run these against YOLO-class detectors, VLM-based approaches (GPT-4o, Gemini),
        and the V-JEPA 2.1 family — the most honest baselines for each capability class.
      </p>
      <p>
        Darwin beats V-JEPA 2.1 on SSv2 and EK-100 action benchmarks at a fraction of
        the training cost. On temporal localization tasks it outperforms every VLM we
        have tested, because VLMs sample frames — Darwin watches video. Honest failure
        modes are part of the published results: low-contrast scenes and heavily
        occluded objects remain harder for Darwin than for specialized detectors.
      </p>

      <div class="link-cards">
        <a class="link-card" href="/blog/darwin-video-jepa-benchmarks">
          <strong>Darwin: Video JEPA model that outperforms SOTA models while running on edge CPU</strong>
          <span>Published benchmark results — the primary reference.</span>
        </a>
        <a class="link-card" href="/blog/benchmark-post">
          <strong>Benchmark post</strong>
          <span>Methodology and extended results.</span>
        </a>
      </div>

      <ComingSoon note="Extended methodology and next model release results — coming during our August launch." />
    </section>
  </div>
</Base>

<style>
  .page { max-width: 760px; margin: 0 auto; padding: 64px 24px 96px; }
  .back { font-size: var(--fs-body-sm); color: var(--color-text-muted); display: block; margin-bottom: 32px; }
  .back:hover { color: var(--color-signal); }
  .hero { margin-bottom: 40px; }
  .eyebrow {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: var(--fs-footnote);
    font-weight: 500;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.1em;
    color: var(--color-signal);
    margin: 0 0 12px;
  }
  h1 { font-size: var(--fs-h1); font-weight: 700; letter-spacing: -0.02em; line-height: 1.2; margin: 0 0 16px; }
  .lede { font-size: var(--fs-body-lg); color: var(--color-text-muted); line-height: 1.6; margin: 0; }
  .content p { font-size: var(--fs-body-lg); line-height: 1.75; color: var(--color-text-primary); opacity: 0.85; margin: 0 0 16px; }

  .link-cards { display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 12px; margin: 32px 0; }
  .link-card {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 4px;
    padding: 16px 20px;
    border: 1px solid var(--color-border);
    border-radius: 6px;
    background: var(--color-bg-surface);
    color: inherit;
    font-size: var(--fs-body-sm);
  }
  .link-card:hover { border-color: rgba(27, 79, 224, 0.4); }
  .link-card strong { color: var(--color-signal); font-weight: 600; }
  .link-card span { color: var(--color-text-muted); }
  @media (max-width: 640px) { h1 { font-size: var(--fs-h2); } .page { padding: 44px 20px 64px; } }
</style>
